1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,008
Same room. Same moment. Two different menus.

2
00:00:03,908 --> 00:00:06,558
The doctor, on the Science console, can read something

3
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:09,631
the engineer, on Engineering, can't,

4
00:00:10,081 --> 00:00:12,743
and neither of them can open the captain's log alone.

5
00:00:14,543 --> 00:00:16,668
That's the whole trick of a boarding party,

6
00:00:17,118 --> 00:00:20,302
and it costs you one word and one semicolon.

7
00:00:21,502 --> 00:00:24,150
Here's the airlock on the Science console's handheld.

8
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,899
Dr Hale has four buttons,

9
00:00:27,349 --> 00:00:32,175
and the first one, Read the name tags on the suits, is new.

10
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:36,103
Chief Okoro, on Engineering, has the other three.

11
00:00:37,903 --> 00:00:40,963
In the file, it's a choice of the kind you already write,

12
00:00:41,413 --> 00:00:43,266
with two things added on the end.

13
00:00:44,166 --> 00:00:46,566
The first is the word if, and then medical.

14
00:00:47,016 --> 00:00:49,804
Only someone whose job is medical is offered this.

15
00:00:50,704 --> 00:00:53,225
That's the word on the Roles line in your roster,

16
00:00:53,675 --> 00:00:56,290
so this one belongs to Dr Hale.

17
00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,490
The second comes after a semicolon.

18
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,497
Learn, and then a name I've made up.

19
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:06,953
When she takes it, the party knows a fact.

20
00:01:08,753 --> 00:01:10,896
And the choice needs somewhere to go,

21
00:01:11,346 --> 00:01:15,482
so I write a short room that says what she found,

22
00:01:15,932 --> 00:01:16,978
with one way back.

23
00:01:17,878 --> 00:01:21,448
On her handheld, that room is the next line on the page,

24
00:01:21,898 --> 00:01:23,820
with one button, Step back.

25
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,289
Then the same again, for the engineer.

26
00:01:28,189 --> 00:01:34,319
In the reactor room, Chief Okoro's handheld offers him a reading, and Dr Hale's doesn't.

27
00:01:36,119 --> 00:01:41,235
In the file, it's a choice in the reactor room that only engineering is offered,

28
00:01:41,685 --> 00:01:43,180
a fact with its own name,

29
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:45,845
and a short room to hold what he reads.

30
00:01:47,645 --> 00:01:51,844
So now each of my two people has one thing that only they can read.

31
00:01:52,744 --> 00:01:56,593
And notice the shape, because you'll use it again and again.

32
00:01:57,043 --> 00:02:00,520
A reading goes somewhere, says one thing, and comes straight back.

33
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:06,850
Now the lock. On the bridge, once both readings are taken,

34
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,548
the handheld offers a new button, Answer the log.

35
00:02:12,348 --> 00:02:15,274
In the file, it's a choice with a different kind of condition.

36
00:02:15,724 --> 00:02:18,613
It says learned, then at least, then two.

37
00:02:20,413 --> 00:02:21,709
Learned is a number.

38
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:25,111
It's how many different facts the party has.

39
00:02:26,011 --> 00:02:28,603
The party, mind, and not the person,

40
00:02:29,053 --> 00:02:32,138
so the surgeon's reading and the engineer's both count.

41
00:02:33,038 --> 00:02:34,482
And a fact counts once,

42
00:02:34,932 --> 00:02:37,284
however many times they read it.

43
00:02:39,084 --> 00:02:41,957
Behind the lock is the last room of this story,

44
00:02:42,407 --> 00:02:44,859
so it's the second room that gets a way home.

45
00:02:46,059 --> 00:02:47,442
There's one more thing to fix.

46
00:02:48,342 --> 00:02:53,031
A party that walks to the bridge first finds a room with nothing to do,

47
00:02:53,481 --> 00:02:55,054
and they'll think the game is broken.

48
00:02:56,854 --> 00:02:58,713
So the handheld tells them.

49
00:02:59,613 --> 00:03:03,418
Too early, the bridge's line says the log is locked behind a question.

50
00:03:03,868 --> 00:03:07,568
Later, the same room says they know what it's going to ask.

51
00:03:09,368 --> 00:03:11,677
In the file, I write the line twice,

52
00:03:12,127 --> 00:03:14,920
with a condition in curly brackets on each.

53
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,788
A room should never leave the party wondering whether it's finished.

54
00:03:19,238 --> 00:03:21,871
If there's more to find, say so in the room.

55
00:03:23,071 --> 00:03:25,563
Three rules. Nobody gets an empty menu,

56
00:03:26,013 --> 00:03:29,220
so every room keeps a choice with no condition.

57
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:32,326
A reading goes somewhere and comes back.

58
00:03:33,226 --> 00:03:34,396
And count your facts:

59
00:03:34,846 --> 00:03:38,611
I have two, and the log asks for two. Lint is clean.

60
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,817
It catches a misspelled learn.

61
00:03:42,267 --> 00:03:44,113
It catches the sign the wrong way round.

62
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:48,544
It does not catch a misspelled job.

63
00:03:48,994 --> 00:03:52,086
It says clean, and nobody is ever offered that reading.

64
00:03:52,986 --> 00:03:55,038
So check that one by eye.

65
00:03:55,488 --> 00:03:58,299
Every word after an if is the word learned,

66
00:03:58,749 --> 00:04:00,102
or a job from your roster.

67
00:04:01,302 --> 00:04:05,179
Two people aboard. The doctor has the button, and the chief doesn't.

68
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:07,277
Straight to the bridge:

69
00:04:07,727 --> 00:04:11,715
no log, and the line says why. Back.

70
00:04:12,165 --> 00:04:14,413
She reads the tags. Aft.

71
00:04:14,863 --> 00:04:17,355
He reads the record. Forward again,

72
00:04:17,805 --> 00:04:20,582
and the line has changed, and there's the log.

73
00:04:21,481 --> 00:04:23,615
Both consoles show the same page,

74
00:04:24,065 --> 00:04:26,893
and either one's button moves the whole party.

75
00:04:28,693 --> 00:04:31,693
Now watch what happens when the doctor stays behind on the ship.

76
00:04:32,593 --> 00:04:34,541
Same room, one person,

77
00:04:34,991 --> 00:04:36,277
and her reading comes to me,

78
00:04:36,727 --> 00:04:39,525
last in the row, marked as covering for medical.

79
00:04:40,425 --> 00:04:42,590
A short crew still finishes the story.

80
00:04:43,490 --> 00:04:46,224
And the covering only happens for a job,

81
00:04:46,674 --> 00:04:50,605
one that's on your roster, or one of the game's standard jobs.

82
00:04:51,505 --> 00:04:54,522
A word that's nobody's job isn't offered to anyone.

83
00:04:55,722 --> 00:04:57,990
Your third crew member has a job you made up.

84
00:04:58,890 --> 00:05:00,909
Give them a reading on the bridge,

85
00:05:01,359 --> 00:05:03,031
and leave the log at two.

86
00:05:03,931 --> 00:05:06,707
Now any two of three readings will open it,

87
00:05:07,157 --> 00:05:09,075
so there's more than one way through.

88
00:05:10,875 --> 00:05:14,367
Next time, we ask not only what someone's job is,

89
00:05:14,817 --> 00:05:16,422
but how good they are at it.
